02:52:23 said  I compared the two apps feature by feature, then added most of the original's design, text and image editing tools to MatCraft. New tools:
02:52:23 said  - **Designs:** select several things at once, group, align and distribute, arrange, flip both ways, cut/copy/paste, weld, combine, slice, attach, flatten, offset, contour, four more operations (Deboss, Wave, Perforate, Guide) and three more shapes.
02:52:23 said  - **Text:** your computer's fonts, bold and italic, letter and line spacing, alignment, curved text, and splitting text into separate letters.
02:52:23 said  - **Images:** SVG, DXF and photo uploads, with background removal, cut-the-outline and print then cut.
02:52:23 said  It builds, the check passes and 14 self-tests pass, but I only looked at pictures of the canvas and text bar. I haven't clicked through weld, slice, offset, contour or the photo-upload window in the running app.
02:52:23 said  It's not a full 1-to-1 yet. The Compare table and comparison document now list 52 features: 27 the same, 13 partly, 9 not yet.
02:52:23 said  - **Partly there:** offset has rounded corners only, background removal works by colour or darkness rather than an eraser, and print then cut saves a page for you to print yourself.
02:52:24 said  - **Not there yet:** the online image library, monogram maker, pen writing fonts, pattern fills, moving pieces on a mat by hand, and actually sending a cut to the machine.
