03:07:21 said  I made the four changes:
03:07:21 said  - **Scrolling:** the mouse wheel now stops at the edges of the design area plus a one-inch margin, so you can't scroll off into empty space.
03:07:21 said  - **Fonts:** the font list now opens with a search box, and the Up/Down arrows (Page Up/Down to jump) change the text on the canvas as you go; Enter keeps the font and Esc goes back.
03:07:21 said  - **Uploads:** you can open your computer's file picker to choose one or several files, or drag files straight onto the window.
03:07:21 said  - **SVG converter:** it turns photos, drawings and DXF files into cut-ready SVG files saved next to the originals. The picture window also has "Save as SVG", the Projects panel can export the whole design as SVG, and SVG files now upload at their real size.
03:07:22 said  The app builds, the check passes, all 18 self-tests pass and the Linux version compiles. The tests cover the scroll limit and converting a real PNG file (with a hole) to SVG and back. I only looked at a picture of the new Upload panel; I couldn't try the file picker, drag and drop or the arrow-key font preview by hand, so the file picker on Bazzite in particular is untested.
