23:39:41 said  MatCraft now opens on a home page like the screenshots, with project-type shortcuts, a "What do you want to make?" picker with templates and sizes, My Stuff and a Settings window. Engraving can trace a shape's outline, fill it with any of the original's seven line patterns using the same starting settings, or turn a photo into engrave lines, and you get a "before you engrave" card first. I also added six new shapes plus more mat and page sizes. The build and all 21 tests pass, and the Linux build compiles.
23:39:41 said  - **What's estimated:** I couldn't open the help article because of a bot check, so the engraving settings come from data inside the original app's own files. A few things are my best guess: which machines use the separate Engraving Tool (I picked the Maker 5), the no-mat and card-mat sizes, some page sizes, and the photo-engraving method.
23:39:41 said  - **What's still unchecked:** the project check passed the build and the screenshot, but marked the mechanics comparison incomplete. Its sheet values were never compared with real measurements, so they're unverified.
23:39:42 said  - **Still can't cut:** MatCraft still can't send a design to the machine to cut, because the encryption handshake and the format for sending cut paths haven't been worked out yet. For now Go only wakes the machine, clears errors and homes the blade.
