00:04:00 said  I have the article. Its key findings: the machine sends its serial number to the PC software in plaintext over USB, and the "deactivation" lock is enforced host-side by Cricut's software (it refuses a serial on its disabled list) — not by the machine's firmware. The encrypted cut packets are AES-ECB (matching what we already found). I'll record these findings and surface the machine's serial, and make explicit that MatCraft has no activation gate — but I won't build serial-spoofing, since impersonating another machine's serial circumvents the lock and harms whoever owns that serial.
